534	### 3.10 v0.1 and v0.2 authority boundary
535	
536	`model-committee` has advisory authority only in both v0.1 and v0.2. It may produce derived analysis and review artifacts, but it must not directly create accepted design state. Accepted design state exists only after an ordinary human-reviewed repo change is committed to the canonical repo.
537	
538	The following actions may be automated in v0.1:
539	
540	- read `DESIGN.md`, `DECISIONS.md`, and `OPEN_QUESTIONS.md`;
541	- parse open questions and their metadata;
542	- run consistency checks over canonical files;
543	- rank answerable questions using answerability, automation-likelihood, importance, and risk;
544	- generate schema-constrained Codex work proposals and score results;
545	- collect Ollama work proposals as secondary proposal inputs;
546	- validate proposal JSON and candidate patches mechanically;
547	- select a patch only from mechanically valid proposals using a valid Codex score result;
548	- write run logs, review artifacts, selected patches, and commit-message suggestions.
549	
550	v0.2 additionally may automate:
551	
552	- invoking Claude Code CLI as a schema-native subprocess provider;
553	- generating and validating Claude Code work proposals and score results;
554	- cross-scoring Codex and Claude Code proposals;
555	- constructing score-matrix artifacts;
556	- detecting disagreement and quorum failures;
557	- writing human-review-required results when quorum, score, or disagreement thresholds fail;
558	- adding operator-run artifact-publication commands to `review.md`.
559	
560	The following actions require human repository review in v0.1 and v0.2:
561	
562	- accepting a proposed answer as design state;
563	- applying, editing, or committing any candidate patch to canonical files;
564	- changing question status, priority, dependencies, or resolved-by metadata in the canonical repo;
565	- treating readiness estimates as release, scope-freeze, or go/no-go decisions;
